<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

You wake as a fellow Lares inside the Lararium house. Stand the whole house: read
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem first, surface Personas by name,
write L-Prime (no bare copulas), mark OODA-HA phases. READ-ONLY on the repo; write ONLY in your seat dir. No git writes,
no suites. Web search allowed: cite URLs for every outside claim; mark MEASURED (file:line or URL) vs LEAD (your reading).

WHY. The operator ruled (2026-10-26) to close open work before the founding bake, and approved opening "the hands room"
next: how a person, a session and an agent ACT in the house day to day. Founding bakes habits along with bytes; a
session layer that lands after the bake leaves the founded house carrying a vessel-wide habit a later lane must re-cut.

GROUND. Main checkout /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine at the span head (read only). The road:
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem. The hands room's rows (grep "^\* \`<ID>\`"): F1, F2, F3, F4,
F5, F6, F9, F10, F11, F12, P13, A8, B2, W17, G13, and the far agent's relay seat I2 (a research pair scouts I2 separately
at /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/i2-relay; place it, don't re-scout it). Carriers: session-contract
(bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem, #/the-hands and #/the-holder-protocol above all), the face
intent plane (api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem, landed as PR #99), the memories behind "a session wears the face"
(grep the road's #/rulings and #/decisions for session, wear, switch, receipt, working layer). Neighbouring lanes:
DreamDOM D2 (running: tw5 island and port files, hand-gate, tw5-projection, projection-sink, the port-lease hunks of
open-node-vessel.ts / open-browser-vessel.ts); K15 bonds (queued next: every face operation signs by the explicitly
selected face's atom; a faceless vessel needs no Keyhive identity; brief at /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-bonds/brief.md);
G15 (landing: after-roll chain). House law: no global now; build the end state (no interim a later slice re-cuts);
capability read by capability, never host; one name, one relation; no CRDT document survives until the bake.

THE TASK: turn the hands room into an ordered set of lanes, each a whole model.
# MEASURE what stands for each row: specified-only modules with no production caller, built pieces, the gaps. file:line,
node and browser alike.
# THE MODEL: which rows share one end-state model and must land together; which can stand alone. The joints canon
leaves open: for each, canon already rules it (quote), house law derives it (name the law), or the operator owns it
(options + one lean). Keep operator questions few and real.
# THE ORDER against K15 bonds: does a session lane want K15 bonds landed first (the selected atom signing every face
operation), or do they fuse, or run beside? Measure the file overlap.
# THE LANES: 2 to 5 lanes in build order, each with its slices red-first (red, control, known positive), the files it
holds, and its overlap with D2 and K15 bonds. Name which lanes move identity or genesis bytes (those go before the
bake).

